# Day 5 - Building Business Logic with Apex

## Topics Learned

### 1. Business Logic
- Business logic is the decision-making part of an application.
- It validates business rules before storing data.
- Without business logic, software only stores information and cannot make decisions.

### 2. Service Classes
Created separate Apex service classes:
- StudentService
- JobService
- ApplicationService

Each service has a single business responsibility.

### 3. Application Workflow
Implemented the following workflow:

Receive Application
↓
Check Duplicate
↓
Validate Deadline
↓
Validate Eligibility
↓
Save Record
↓
Return Result

### 4. Apex Concepts Used
- Apex Classes
- Apex Methods
- SOQL
- DML
- Helper Methods
- Trigger Handler
- Validation Logic

### 5. Business Validations
Implemented:
- Duplicate Application Check
- CGPA Validation
- Active Backlogs Validation
- Graduation Year Validation
- Application Deadline Validation

### 6. Engineering Principles Learned
- One Service = One Responsibility
- Build incrementally
- Separate business logic from UI
- Use meaningful method names
- Write reusable helper methods
